  "claim": "A member team of the 2009 Big East Conference football season played and won on on December 19. In this game played the future Atlanta Falcons wide receiver teenager Mohamed Sanu Sr was the game's MVP.",
  "evidencia": "Page: 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl. Sentence: The 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl presented by Beef 'O' Brady's, formerly known as the St. Petersburg Bowl, was the second edition of the college football bowl game and was played at Tropicana Field in St. Petersburg, Florida.\nPage: 2009 St. Petersburg Bowl. Sentence: Rutgers defeated UCF 45–24 in a game where Mohamed Sanu, the game's MVP, caught 4 passes for 97 yards and a touchdown in addition to rushing 14 times for 47 yards and two touchdowns.\nPage: Mohamed Sanu. Sentence: Mohamed Sanu Sr. (born August 22, 1989) is an American football wide receiver for the Atlanta Falcons of the National Football League (NFL).\nPage: 2009 Rutgers Scarlet Knights football team. Sentence: The Scarlet Knights finished the season 9–4, 3–4 in Big East play and won the St. Petersburg Bowl, 45–24, over UCF.\nPage: 2009 Big East Conference football season. Sentence: The Big East Conference consists of 8 football members: Cincinnati, Connecticut, Louisville, Pittsburgh, Rutgers, South Florida, Syracuse, and West Virginia.",
